      "name": "registry-authority-contract",
      "title": "External registry — confirming a source's authority",
      "description": "The contract the `external-registry` role is held to when a candidate source is checked against the body that publishes it: resolve the identifier through its own API and return the record, so authority is a resolved fact. When the answer is uncertain or absent the verdict is not invented here; the work plan records the citation as unverified. A role played by an external party is held to a contract, not handed instructions.",
